{"skill":{"slug":"adaptive-reasoning","displayName":"Adaptive Reasoning"},"version":{"version":"1.0.0","createdAt":1770547044848,"changelog":"- Initial release of adaptive-reasoning skill.\n- Automatically assesses incoming requests for complexity and dynamically adjusts reasoning depth.\n- Uses a scoring system (0–10) based on factors such as multi-step logic, ambiguity, code architecture, math, novelty, and stakes.\n- Visual indicators (`🧠`, `🧠🔥`) show when advanced reasoning is active.\n- Activates reasoning mode without user intervention; reverts to fast mode for simple tasks.\n- Includes clear guidance on when not to escalate and when to downgrade reasoning for efficiency.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3525,"sha256":"fa28dbbf0534df2eec56388607935732bc41c7e0f248e518ff9ec00f993a72e3","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":1833,"sha256":"45e71410e7cbd8adaaeaf63ea27600304dde6276771e1d7b87f8f1a8b78380b4","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789039470736,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"9846862cb8db0ea4137bdb75396ac181320778a033927d75103b533c8517c331","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/9846862cb8db0ea4137bdb75396ac181320778a033927d75103b533c8517c331","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: adaptive-reasoning\nVersion: 1.0.0\n\nThe 'adaptive-reasoning' skill is designed to enhance the AI agent's performance by dynamically adjusting its internal reasoning level based on task complexity. All instructions within SKILL.md, including those that modify the agent's internal state (e.g., `/reasoning on`, `session_status` tool) and output (appending icons), are directly aligned with this stated purpose. There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or any other harmful intent; the 'prompt injection' aspects are for self-regulation and meta-cognition, not for malicious manipulation.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779162191932},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":38,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789039470736},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"The skill does not access files or send data out, but it broadly and silently changes agent reasoning behavior and response formatting across user messages.","dimensions":[{"detail":"For a mental preprocessing skill, automatically invoking session_status or slash-style reasoning commands is overbroad and not clearly user-directed.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The inspected package contains only artifact/SKILL.md and no install scripts, dependencies, executables, remote fetches, or code payloads.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"The skill says it triggers on every user message, uses subjective scoring, says 'Do not ask. Just activate.', and requires icons at the end of responses, which can conflict with user-requested output formats.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"No OS persistence, credential access, filesystem mutation, or network behavior is present, but the skill does attempt current-session reasoning-state changes and optional silent downgrade behavior.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is adaptive reasoning, but the artifact goes beyond advisory guidance by directing automatic reasoning-mode changes and required response suffixes for broad categories of requests.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Review before installing. This skill is not showing data theft or local system access, but it can silently affect how the agent handles many requests, change reasoning state, increase token use, and append icons to responses without asking. Install only if you want that automatic behavior, and prefer a version that requires explicit user opt-in for session-level changes.","findings":"[SQP-1] unexpected: The broad every-message trigger is artifact-backed and materially over-scoped for an advisory reasoning helper, even though it is not malicious by itself.\n[SQP-1] expected: A complexity scoring rubric is expected for this purpose, but its subjective boundaries increase over-application risk when paired with automatic session changes.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The mandatory visible response markers are not necessary for adaptive reasoning and may interfere with user or platform output requirements.\n[T01] unexpected: The static scan concern is supported by artifact text directing silent reasoning-mode changes and forced output formatting, but there is no evidence of exfiltration, destructive behavior, or persistence.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789039470736}}}}}